# =============================================================================
# This repository tracks ONLY the NextScan/ engine tree (user decision,
# 2026-08-22). Everything else in the working directory stays on disk but is
# deliberately outside version control.
#
# Whitelist approach: ignore every root entry, then re-allow NextScan/ and
# this file. The exclusions further down still apply INSIDE NextScan/ (they
# are unanchored patterns), which keeps build output out of the repo.
# =============================================================================

/*
!/.gitignore
!/NextScan/

# --- build output / runtime data (applies inside NextScan/ too) ---
bin/
out/
scans/
tmp/
__pycache__/
scan_log.txt

# compiled binaries anywhere in the tree
*.exe
*.dll
*.obj
*.pdb

# --- logs & generated diagnostics ---
*_log.txt
exe_log.txt
diag_report.txt

# --- credentials & session state: never commit, in any tree ---
keys.txt
keystate.txt
puter_token.txt
setup_puter.bat
chrome_profile/

# --- bulky / re-downloadable runtime assets (relevant only if the
#     whitelist is ever widened again) ---
node/
models/
profiles/
Cdp/
queue/
fixqueue/
debug/
backup/

# personal photos processed by the fix tools; keep only the source snapshot
backup_original/*
!backup_original/scanhelper.cs.pre-native
